msgstr "Qiskit Runtime client 0.46.0 {#qiskit-runtime-client-0460}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "April 2026 {#april-2026}"
msgstr "April 2026 {#april-2026}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<span id=\"executor-primitive\"></span>\n"
"- **Introducing the Executor primitive**: We're excited to announce the release of the new `Executor` primitive and a new version of the noise-learning helper class, `NoiseLearnerV3`, both of which were first previewed at QDC 2025.\n"
msgstr ""
"<span id=\"executor-primitive\"></span>\n"
"- **Einführung des Executor Primitive**: Wir freuen uns, die Veröffentlichung des neuen `Executor` Primitive und einer neuen Version der Noise-Learning-Hilfsklasse, `NoiseLearnerV3`, bekanntzugeben, die beide erstmals auf der QDC 2025 vorgestellt wurden.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Together with [Samplomatic](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/index.html), they make up the [directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model), which provides full transparency and control to fine-tune your error mitigation workflow. The [Probabilistic error cancellation with shaded lightcones](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-slc/tutorials/01_getting_started.html) tutorial, for example, demonstrates how this model is used to combine advanced techniques, including shaded lightcones, probabilistic error cancellation (PEC), Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX), and [measurement-based postselection](/guides/post-selection), to further improve the result quality.\n"
msgstr "  Zusammen mit [Samplomatic](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/index.html) bilden sie das [gesteuerte Ausführungsmodell](/guides/directed-execution-model), das vollständige Transparenz und Kontrolle bietet, um deinen Fehlermitigation-Workflow fein abzustimmen. Das Tutorial [Probabilistic error cancellation with shaded lightcones](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-slc/tutorials/01_getting_started.html) zeigt beispielsweise, wie dieses Modell verwendet wird, um fortgeschrittene Techniken zu kombinieren, darunter Shaded Lightcones, probabilistische Fehlerauslöschung (PEC), Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX) und [messungsbasierte Nachselektion](/guides/post-selection), um die Ergebnisqualität weiter zu verbessern.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  If you prefer a higher level of abstraction, [`EstimatorV2`](/guides/estimator-noise-management) in Qiskit Runtime continues to provide several built-in error mitigation and suppression techniques, which you can easily tune using the [`resilience_level`](/guides/estimator-noise-management#resilience-level) option.\n"
msgstr "  Wenn du eine höhere Abstraktionsebene bevorzugst, bietet [`EstimatorV2`](/guides/estimator-noise-management) in Qiskit Runtime weiterhin mehrere integrierte Fehlermitigation- und -unterdrückungstechniken, die du einfach über die Option [`resilience_level`](/guides/estimator-noise-management#resilience-level) anpassen kannst.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  To learn more, see the following guides:\n"
msgstr "  Weitere Informationen findest du in den folgenden Guides:\n"

